From 0d785e9d8d15b7325b8dc308f0a5eee81064213a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:50:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test: qsa_vbatch_parity compares the attention with
 STRATA_ATTN_VBATCH off, 8 and 4 cells bitwise

The existing parity tests cannot see the batched value loop: qsa_slots_parity compares slots against
per-row calls, kv_stream_parity streamed against resident, each through the same body.  This one
switches the loop in one process (qsa_decode_attn_set_vbatch) and memcmps the attention output and the
per-chunk partials (acc, max, sum) of qsa_decode_attn_batch, qsa_decode_attn_slots and
qsa_decode_attn_step: KV formats fp16, int8, q4_0 and int8-K/q4_0-V; 1/2/4/8 rows; contexts 1 to
190000 cells (chunk tails of 1, 3, 7, 8, 9, 37, 63 and 64 cells); with and without non-resident pages
at a group's first, middle and last cell, a whole masked group and a masked tail.  The ctest runs it
twice, the second time with STRATA_ATTN_LANECELL=1.  Synthetic data, no model; skips (77) without a
CUDA device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
